2026-09-24  Alexander Karlberg  <alexander.karlberg@mpp.mpg.de>

	* src/inclusive/nonfact.f90 (angular_integrals):
	The triangle integrals (t01, t022) are computed in the same adaptive
	integration as the first box integrals for each boson (they share
	the roots r1-r4 and their logs): 15% fewer operations in the NF
	angular integrals.

	* src/inclusive/{nonfact.f90|nonfact_expressions.f|incl_parameters.f90|matrix_element.f90}:
	* docs/provbfhh-doc.{tex|pdf}:
	New input nf_regfact: gluon-mass regulator of the non-factorisable
	corrections, lambda = nf_regfact * MV^2 (default 1, as before). The
	integrals multiplying log(lambda/MV^2) are obtained from the 1-loop
	ones (b12 = -2 b01, t12 = -2 t01 pointwise), so any lambda costs the
	same; the result does not depend on it.

	* src/inclusive/nonfact.f90:
	* src/inclusive/nonfact_expressions.f (box_integrands):
	The 1-loop and 2-loop box integrals (b01, b022), which share the
	roots and logs, are computed together in one vector-valued adaptive
	integration and cached for the second call with the same arguments.
	HH NF runs are about 1.6 times faster again (7 times in total).

	* src/inclusive/nonfact.f90:
	* src/inclusive/incl_parameters.f90:
	* docs/*-doc.tex, docs/*-doc.pdf:
	The azimuthal integrals of the non-factorisable corrections used RK4
	with niter = 100 steps (400 integrand calls per integral; since the
	integrands do not depend on y this is Simpson's rule with half of
	the calls repeated). They now use adaptive Gauss-Kronrod (7-15)
	quadrature with relative accuracy nf_epsrel (new input, default
	1e-8), typically 70-110 calls, and much more accurate at large
	transverse momenta, where the integrands are sharply peaked (RK4 was
	off by up to 16% there). The integrals multiplied by log(lambda/MV^2)
	are skipped, since lambda = MV^2. niter is no longer used. The NF runs
	are 4-5 times faster.

	* src/inclusive/nonfact_expressions.f:
	The roots r1-r6 and the integrands of the non-factorisable
	corrections were complex*8, i.e. single precision (effect on the
	angular integrals: typically 5e-9, at most 2e-4). Now complex*16.

	* Makefile:
	Build on macOS: the Fortran module directory flag (-J) is no longer
	passed to the C++ compiler (clang++ rejects it), and combine_runs is
	linked without -mcmodel=large on macOS (not supported there with the
	position-independent code that is the default, and not needed).

	* src/inclusive/tensor.f90:
	* src/inclusive/matrix_element.f90 (trace_matrix):
	Use error stop, so that fatal errors give a non-zero exit status.

	* src/inclusive/matrix_element.f90 (eval_matrix_element_tensor):
	The tensor matrix element now combines the perturbative orders like
	the analytic one (products of beam-1 order i and beam-2 order j with
	i + j = n + 1, n = order_start..order_stop). Before, it summed the
	structure functions over all orders up to order_stop and contracted
	the product, which added beyond-accuracy terms (NLO x NLO at NLO,
	etc.: +2.7e-4 of sigma at NLO, 0.65e-4 at NNLO) and ignored
	order_start. The hadronic tensors are expanded in three basis
	tensors (hadronic_basis) whose contractions with the current are
	computed once per point (trace_matrix, on plain 4x4 arrays), and the
	orders are combined with the structure functions (order_sum). With
	zero widths, same-seed runs with and without the tensor matrix
	element now give identical results at every order.

	* src/inclusive/matrix_element.f90:
	cmplx() without kind=dp returns a single-precision complex, so the
	propagators of both the analytic and the tensor matrix element were
	rounded to single precision (relative effect about 1e-8). Added
	kind=dp throughout.

	* src/inclusive/matrix_element.f90
	(eval_matrix_element_tensor, VVtoHH_tensor):
	Fixed the F3 terms of the tensor matrix element. The four-vectors
	were stored with their contravariant components in tensors declared
	with lower indices, i.e. as the parity-flipped vectors, while the
	Levi-Civita tensor of the F3 part of the hadronic tensor was not
	flipped. This gave wrong F3 x F3 interference terms between the
	g^mu_nu and the t/u-channel parts of the VV -> HH current (about
	1e-4 of the cross section; the F1 and F2 terms were not affected).
	The vectors are now lowered with the metric. With zero widths the
	tensor and the analytic (default) matrix element now agree to
	machine precision, F3 included. The analytic F3F3 expression in
	ME_expressions.f was correct.
	This also affects the non-factorisable corrections, which always use
	the tensor matrix element.

	* src/inclusive/tensor.f90:
	Replaced by the allocation-free version shared with proVBFH and
	proVBFH-inclusive (same interface and results; see the
	proVBFH-inclusive ChangeLog and its "make check").
	Added InitFourVector.

